 "text": "Hi, how are you doing these days? Once upon a moonlit night, a brave little wood bird flew into a dark forest. She was looking for her missing friends, birds that had disappeared together. In the gloom, she flopped down on cold branch and huddled down, scared but determined. She sang soft song to herself, and listened for answers. After a while, she heard a single bird call, deep in the trees. She followed it, step by trepid step, Of course. In the middle of night, when the moon was high over the ocean, a little mouse tapped at the window with her tusks, and whispered through the gap that she had food for the bird, and would keep the other creatures quiet.",
